WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.350
The SCP Foundation has dealt with plenty of
things that no one could ever even imagine,

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.860
creatures and objects beyond anyone’s wildest
dreams.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:15.650
An evil old man that can walk through walls,
an Ikea that never ends, a giant underwater

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:20.460
eel that can erase your memories, and so much
more.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:25.789
But sometimes, the anomalies they discover
seem to be plucked from a familiar nightmare.

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:31.119
In Korea, shortly after the end of the Second
World War, a team of SCP Foundation officers

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:35.300
encountered something right out of a dark,
twisted fairytale.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.530
In the late 1940s, the fifth squad of the
Eastern Division of the SCP Foundation, received

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:46.820
a call to come to Busan, Korea, and investigate
a potential anomaly involving several deaths.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:52.390
Three agents, referred to from now on as Agent
One, Agent Two, and Agent Three, were deployed

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:56.379
to the region, where they first headed to
the morgue to examine the bodies under the

00:00:56.379 --> 00:00:59.269
cover of reporters investigating the deaths.

00:00:59.269 --> 00:01:02.410
The nature of the wounds indicated an animal
attack.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:06.750
An eyewitness account from an old woman who
saw a fox-like creature eating one of her

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.600
cows supported this hypothesis.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.460
Of course, the agents knew differently.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:17.450
Sure, it was something like an animal, but
this culprit was no animal they had ever encountered.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:22.380
The three recounted stories of fox spirits,
villainous tricksters, capable of changing

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:27.370
their shape and oppressing all kinds of havoc
on those unfortunate souls they targeted.

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:32.390
While sweeping the area, the agents encountered
a beautiful young woman sitting under a waterfall,

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:33.840
combing her hair.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.930
She was dressed in a light robe, and her feet
were bare.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.939
This, they noticed, gave her away.

00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:44.440
Instead of having human feet, she had paws
covered in reddish fur.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:48.810
The agents assumed that this creature was
inexperienced, unable to properly conceal

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:49.810
herself.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.430
They believed they had the upper hand on her.

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:55.500
They would soon see the error of their ways.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:00.380
The woman greeted the three men and invited
them to have dinner at her nearby cottage.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.980
Believing themselves to be relatively safe,
armed as they were and with three people against

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.880
one delicate - if inhuman - woman, they agreed.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:14.330
The fox woman ushered them to a lovely, rustic
cottage and sat them down at the dining table.

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:18.640
She served them plum wine, rice, pickled turnips,
and meat.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:23.570
Everything was delicious, and, feeling at
ease, the agents decided to turn in for the

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:24.570
night.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.500
This creature, though unusual, did not seem
threatening.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.310
She had no reason to attack them, or so they
thought.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:35.150
Agent One woke in the night to go to the bathroom
and tiptoed out of the cottage to relieve

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.720
himself behind a bush.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.610
There, he saw Agent Two with the fox woman.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.330
Let’s just say…they were getting to know
each other intimately.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:47.140
Suddenly, in an abrupt change of mood, she
bit him.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:51.030
She tore the man’s throat out with her teeth
before he could scream, turning his cries

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:53.020
to a wet, useless gurgle.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:58.060
Then, she took her hand and plunged it into
his belly, shredding the flesh with razor-sharp

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.150
claws.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.650
He thrashed and tried to fight her off, but
she shoved him to the ground and tore his

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:06.170
stomach open, rooting around inside for something.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:10.340
When she found it, she stopped and gleefully
tore out his liver.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.540
As the first agent looked on in horror, she
lifted his colleague’s liver and swallowed

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.260
it whole in one single gulp.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:21.790
Not noticing her onlooker, she continued her
vile work, peeling her victim’s skin like

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:22.900
an orange.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:27.450
The agent who witnessed the whole thing regained
his ability to move, adrenaline flooding his

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:31.950
veins, and ran back to the cottage in search
of his remaining teammate.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.840
Agent One shook Agent Three awake, babbling
incoherently as he tried to explain what was

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:41.560
going on, and the fact that they needed to
leave and they needed to leave now.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:46.810
To his shock, Agent Two walked into the room,
asking what all the noise was about.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.680
Agent One immediately noticed the man’s
glowing yellow eyes and made his next move

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:51.830
without thinking.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.810
He pulled out his gun and fired.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:57.270
Agent Three drew his weapon next, pointing
it at One and yelling for him to put the weapon

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.270
away.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:02.950
One tried to explain that this man was not
their friend, but rather the fox in disguise,

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:04.620
but he wouldn’t listen.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:07.970
The fox grabbed One, and Three shot him in
the upper arm.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:12.020
Agent One dropped to the ground, wailing in
pain, as the fox laughed in a high-pitched

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.680
devilish whine.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.200
Agent One scrambled away, crawling into the
living room and slamming the rice paper-screened

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.200
door shut.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.640
There, laid out on the dining table, was another
agent.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:26.990
They had seen this man at the base of the
mountain only a few days ago, but now, here

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:31.950
he was, eyes wide and glassy and skin flayed
open.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.630
Then, Agent One saw the remains of their dinner.

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:37.910
In the bowls, there was the flesh of their
fallen colleague.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:43.090
With it was not rice, but maggots, crawling
over the meat.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:46.730
Agent One was able to improvise a weapon,
breaking off a portion of a wooden beam and

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:50.710
stabbing the fox through the stomach as she
lunged through the rice paper door.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:55.080
He made his way through the forest, running
as fast as he could with his gunshot wound.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.200
He found his way to the bank of the river
and attempted to cross.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:03.540
However, he was disoriented and afraid, it
was pitch black outside, and he was nauseous

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:04.770
from the pain.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:08.290
He slipped on the wet rocks, and hit his head,
falling into the water.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:13.290
The rapids carried him away, pulling him downstream
for half a mile before he was able to grab

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.840
hold of an exposed branch.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.980
Agent One made his way back to his team’s
van, broke a window, and pulled a flamethrower

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:20.980
from the back.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:25.600
He recalled legends about similar fox-like
creatures mentioning an aversion to fire,

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:29.610
and so he prepared to fight her off with as
much as he could get.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:34.500
Just as he readied the flamethrower for use,
the fox woman emerged from the tree line.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:38.790
What happened next is unknown, lost from the
official record.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:44.160
However, after several days, a retrieval team
tracked down Agent One and rescued him, capturing

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.020
the fox woman in the process.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:50.500
He was taken to the hospital, where he remained
with a serious infection for several days

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.260
before he was discharged.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:55.530
Initially, the Foundation planned to terminate
the creature.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:58.730
However, Agent One vehemently opposed that
decision.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:01.020
He insisted that they should keep her alive.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:05.310
He also recommended the containment methods
used to imprison her be adjusted.

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:09.510
The Agent promised that she would not be held
by the chosen methods and that the result

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.200
of her inevitable escape would be devastating.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:16.310
In his official interview, he had this to
say on the subject: “Like I said, she's

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:17.440
spiteful.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:20.670
Every little slight in her eyes she saves
up, and the only way she knows how to repay

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.670
an insult is death.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:27.370
Chaining her to the wall like an animal…
when she gets out, and she will get out, she's

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:30.500
going to kill everyone who had the slightest
thing to do with it.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.150
She won't settle for anything else.”

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:36.670
Much to the Foundation’s surprise, Agent
One visited the fox woman in her holding cell

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:38.040
several times.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:42.350
The Foundation attempted to understand this
concerning behavior, but Agent One refused

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:44.840
to admit that there was anything strange about
it.

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:49.790
His attachment to the fox woman had been attributed
to Stockholm Syndrome, brought on as a result

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:52.730
of several days in the woods spent as her
captive.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:57.050
To this day, Agent One is the only person
to survive that long alone with the creature

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:01.680
that is now known as SCP-953.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:06.380
SCP-953 is a female red fox, weighing approximately
8 kg.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:11.330
Unlike an ordinary fox, her spine splits at
the base into nine different tails.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:16.530
Previously referred to as a kitsune, the shapeshifting
fox spirit of Japanese legend, it has since

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:22.280
been discovered that she is actually a kumiho,
a Korean fox spirit with similar qualities.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:28.889
SCP-953 is a polymorph, also known as a shapeshifter,
though she retains some aspects of her fox-like

00:07:28.889 --> 00:07:35.200
appearance no matter what form she is in,
including ears, paws, tails, eyes, and fur.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:39.889
Though she attempts to cover these revealing
physical traits with clothes and hairstyling,

00:07:39.889 --> 00:07:42.400
she is unable to get rid of them entirely.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:47.650
In addition to her shapeshifting, 953 has
potent psychic abilities including the powers

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.930
of suggestion and telepathy.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:53.880
She has used these abilities to wreak havoc
on her victims, causing them to experience

00:07:53.880 --> 00:08:00.650
terrifying hallucinations, hurt themselves,
and, in one particularly horrific case, convincing

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:04.650
a mother to kill, cook, and eat her own child.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:09.600
She has also successfully used these abilities
to escape containment six times.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:14.820
SCP-953’s most recent escape caused the
deaths of ten Foundation staff.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:19.240
After destroying nearby security cameras,
she shifted into the appearance of an adult

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:23.139
man, walking out the front door in a stolen
lab coat.

00:08:23.139 --> 00:08:27.210
Anyone who stopped her to ask for identification
was swiftly slaughtered.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:31.201
After her escape, the fox disappeared for
five years until she resurfaced at Yiffcon,

00:08:31.201 --> 00:08:37.289
a convention for furries and anthropomorphic
animal enthusiasts.

00:08:37.289 --> 00:08:42.340
There, the fox-like ears and tail that might
draw attention in other places allowed her

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:43.750
to hide in plain sight.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:47.800
The Foundation was alerted to her presence
when a terrified hotel housekeeper called

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:54.310
911, after walking in on SCP-953 slicing open
the torso of a dead convention-goer.

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:58.780
By the time the Foundation reached the convention
center and captured the fox, she had left

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.920
two dozen corpses in her wake.

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:05.460
The bodies, all mutilated almost beyond recognition,
were found scattered throughout the hotel

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:10.150
in various places, including: stuffed into
a mattress, hanging over a shower curtain

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:14.279
rod, rolled up in a carpet, and strewn across
a banquet table.

00:09:14.279 --> 00:09:18.150
The survivors were given Class-A Amnestics
to wipe their memories, and released from

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:19.150
custody.

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:23.210
The convention was cut short, with a dangerous
gas leak as the cover story.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:26.660
So far, the fox has not escaped Foundation
custody again.

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:32.500
SCP-953 is kept in a Type 4 containment cell
in Hallway 99 of Site-17.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:37.890
She is provided 1.5 kg of fresh liver every
day to eat, as well as clean drinking water

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:41.370
and a futon with blankets and sheets that
are changed out weekly.

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:46.390
In exchange for good behavior, she is provided
the occasional luxury item such as plum wine,

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:49.420
novels, or a variety of Korean sweets.

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:54.100
After so many successful escapes, the Foundation
realized that simple physical containment

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:59.040
was not adequate to keep SCP-953 away from
the general population.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:04.070
Making use of her fear of dogs, the Foundation
keeps 953’s containment chamber surrounded

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:08.589
by dog kennels filled with Korean Jindo and
American Foxhounds.

00:10:08.589 --> 00:10:13.570
All staff assigned to SCP-953’s containment
chamber are to be given background checks,

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:17.280
looking for any prior ties to the furry community.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:22.810
Such affiliations may make them vulnerable
to SCP-953’s influence, and have been attributed

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.050
to the death of one Agent Gallagher.

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:29.680
Because of her psychic abilities, no direct
contact with 953 is allowed.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:34.830
All communication with the fox must take place
from a distance of 100 meters, and food, water,

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:38.630
and other items are delivered to her via a
robotic assistant.

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:42.760
She must be considered armed and dangerous
at all times and can only be transported while

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:45.830
accompanied by six members of armed personnel.

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:49.940
There are folklore-based procedures in place
for employees as well, providing specific

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:53.480
instructions to staff assigned to SCP-953.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:58.660
No matter how odd or ridiculous these instructions
may seem, the staff is to adhere to them and

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:04.220
remember that what we might think of as classic
fairytales are often more like ancient Special

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:05.960
Containment Procedures.

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:11.110
If versions of the kumiho and the kitsune
exist, then who knows what other seemingly

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:15.520
mythical creatures the SCP Foundation might
encounter in the future?

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:21.160
What other beasts are lurking on the edges
of civilization, hiding in the shadows, or

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:25.220
worse, hiding in plain sight just under our
noses?

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:31.660
Best to brush up on your local folklore, just
in case, and be careful out there.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:37.950
Now go check out “SCP-3663 - TUNNEL MONSTER”
and “SCP-2430 - Immortal Hitler Clone”

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:39.990
for more haunting anomalous humanoids!

